You'll get at least 5 more wishes from the castle wand, so I would use
these to make sure you get there.
You have Magic Resistance and Reflection, so you're fine there (though
I would hae wished for SDSM + CoMR).

The first thing you need is protection.  Obviously, the Master Key is
one way to help this (just make sure you have enough hitpoints).
Another option is getting a magic marker and enchanting all the armor
you plan to keep for your ascention run (the boots, for example.  The
GDSM as well, unless you're planning on changing at some point).

Regardless of wishes, have you gotten divine protection yet?

Someone else pointed out that you can find lots of goodies on the
castle/Votd levels and that maybe you should hold off your wishing
until then.  Normally this is not a bad idea, but you have more than
enough wishes to get everything, so why not make sure?

Helmet - I would wish for a Helm of Telepathy.  The better to see your
enemies from far off (so you can pelt them with arrows).

Gloves - You're an Orc, so you never get over 18\50 strength.  Getting
Gauntlets of Power (don't forget "blessed fixed") would be useful.

Finally, the Cloak of Displacement is nice, but only MC 2.  I would
consider getting MC 3 soon (though Stormbringer does give you drain
resistance).

Other useful ideas:

- Magicbane is nice, but has the potential to zap you every time you
wield it.  I would with for a blessed fixed +2 athame, so you can
write the 'E' word any time you want.  It will save you when
surrounded.  If you genocide 'L', then you don't have to worry too
much from curses.

- A figurine of an archon can be fun (make sure you have a magic
whistle), but I wouldn't bother.  At this point you should be powerful
enough to do everything yourself.  You're even chaotic, so you can
kill all the town guards and shopkeepers without serious sideffects
(and EAT them!).

Other things you might want later on (but I would hold off on wishing
just yet):

- Ring of conflict.  (For crowd control)
- Ring of slow digestion. (but by this point you should have any
problem with food anyway).
- Ring of levitation. (Or just wait and see if you get it by the time
you hit the castle).


Finally, just a general piece of advice.  Go to the mines, get
protection, power up (AC to -20 at least, good weapon), and get
yourself a luckstone.  Then go directly to the castle.  One thing I've
learned is that doing the castle early really helps.

Dig down at medusa.  Watch out for Minotaurs (keep a wand of teleport
handy for this).  Use Elbereth early and often.  Find out the tune and
crush your enemies.

Think before you act.

